##############################################################
# YSUBITM - entry points of the standard process SUBITM (products)
#
# Purpose
#   BEFWRIITF ("before write to the ITMFACILIT table", called when a product-site
#   is auto-generated at product creation, i.e. a single stock-managed site):
#   write one audit row each time into the custom table YITFLOG, inside the
#   standard transaction. If the audit row
#   cannot be written, GOK = 0 makes the standard abandon the transaction.
#   Every other SUBITM entry point falls through untouched.
#
# Context documented on the SUBITM page (ADC_SUBITM.htm) for BEFWRIITF
#   - one transaction in progress: never Trbegin / Commit / Rollback here
#   - no log file open
#   - ITMMASTER [ITM] open with significant content; GOK = 0 interrupts
#   Y_LOG_ITF opens YITFLOG with Local File inside that transaction, which
#   4gl_file.html allows; see version-caveats.md and test it on your folder.
#
# Prerequisites
#   - GESATB: table YITFLOG, abbreviation YIF, index YIF0 on YLOGID (long integer);
#     fields YLOGID, ITMREF, YUSR, YDAT
#   - GESAPE line: standard script SUBITM, specific script YSUBITM,
#     activity code YITM (X/Y/Z code: protected, switchable)
#   - GESACV: create activity code YITM; activate it in GESADS (Specific tab)
#     and revalidate the folder (personalisation-activity.md)
#
# References: entry-points.md, database.md (adxlog idiom), classic-objects.md (GOK)
##############################################################

$ACTION
  Case ACTION
    When "BEFWRIITF" : Gosub Y_BEFWRIITF
  Endcase
Return

$Y_BEFWRIITF
  # Runs inside the standard program: no Local here, the work is in a Funprog
  If func YSUBITM.Y_LOG_ITF([F:ITM]ITMREF, GUSER) <> [V]CST_AOK
    GOK = 0
  Endif
Return

##############################################################
# Y_LOG_ITF - audit row; joins the standard transaction (adxlog = 1 here),
# and still works if called from code with no transaction open
##############################################################
Funprog Y_LOG_ITF(ITEM, USR)
Value Char ITEM(), USR()
Local File YITFLOG [YIF]
Local Shortint TRANS_OPEN
  Raz [F:YIF]
  [F:YIF]YLOGID = uniqid([YIF])
  [F:YIF]ITMREF = [L]ITEM
  [F:YIF]YUSR   = [L]USR
  [F:YIF]YDAT   = date$
  [L]TRANS_OPEN = adxlog
  If [L]TRANS_OPEN = 0 : Trbegin [YIF] : Endif
  Write [YIF]
  If fstat
    If [L]TRANS_OPEN = 0 and adxlog = 1 : Rollback : Endif
    End [V]CST_AERROR
  Endif
  If [L]TRANS_OPEN = 0 : Commit : Endif
End [V]CST_AOK
